class	equivocation
at	S39	Then the living, whether things or persons, Cebes, are generated from the dead?
fault	"generated from its opposite" holds of comparatives (larger from smaller) and is extended to contradictories (living, dead), where it does not
reference	D. Gallop, Plato: Phaedo (1975), notes on 70c-72e
